  "fanTake": "Well, that was a thoroughly deflating way to start the season. The Patriots trudged into Seattle and left with a 13-10 loss that felt like leaving money on the table—we had our opportunities in the red zone but couldn't capitalize when it mattered most, managing just one touchdown on two trips while coughing up the ball three times overall. Our offense was sluggish (negative EPA), our defense got gashed enough to matter (allowing positive EPA), and third-down efficiency was a disaster (5 for 16 when league average sits around 40%). Rhamondre Stevenson, for all his effort, couldn't reverse the tide. Welcome to 2026, folks—hopefully this is rock bottom.",
